[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:81. Escape]
[00:00.600]Passage 81 | 文章八十一
[00:02.755]Escape | 逃跑
[00:04.915]When he had killed the guard, | 当他杀死看守后，
[00:08.080]the prisoner of war quickly dragged him into the bushes. | 那个战俘迅速将他拖入灌木丛中。
[00:12.570]Working rapidly in the darkness, | 在黑暗中迅速行动，
[00:15.665]he soon changed into the dead man's clothes. | 他很快换上了死者的衣服。
[00:19.715]Now, | 现在，
[00:21.215]dressed in a blue uniform and with a rifle over his shoulders, | 穿着蓝色制服，肩上扛着步枪，
[00:26.060]the prisoner marched boldly up and down in front of the camp. | 那个战俘大胆地在营地前走来走去。
[00:31.220]He could hear shouting in the camp itself. | 他能听到营地里传来叫喊声。
[00:34.880]Lights were blazing, | 灯火通明，
[00:36.960]and men were running here and there. | 人们四处奔跑。
[00:39.565]They had just discovered that a prisoner had escaped. | 他们刚刚发现一名囚犯越狱了。
[00:44.190]At that moment, | 就在那时，
[00:46.290]a large black car with four officers inside it, | 一辆载有四名军官的黑色轿车，
[00:50.585]stopped at the camp gates. | 停在了营地大门前。
[00:53.135]The officers got out, | 军官们下了车，
[00:55.465]and the prisoner stood to attention and saluted as they passed. | 战俘立正敬礼，看着他们走过。
[01:01.040]When they had gone, | 当他们离开后，
[01:03.605]the driver of the car came towards him. | 汽车司机朝他走来。
[01:07.070]The man obviously wanted to talk. | 这个人显然想说话。
[01:10.440]He was rather elderly with grey hair and clear blue eyes. | 他年纪相当大，头发灰白，眼睛湛蓝清澈。
[01:17.045]The prisoner | 那个战俘
[01:18.975]felt sorry for him. | 为他感到惋惜。
[01:20.940]But there was nothing else he could do. | 但他别无选择。
[01:24.230]As the man came near, | 当那个人靠近时，
[01:26.880]the prisoner knocked him to the ground with a sharp blow. | 战俘用一个猛击把他打倒在地。
[01:30.885]Then, | 然后，
[01:32.105]jumping into the car, | 他跳进车里，
[01:33.800]he drove off as quickly as he could. | 以最快的速度开车走了。